{#
  module/Books/view/books/books/book-list.phtml, ported — the physical copies of a
  publication held in the library catalogues the visitor may see.

  Expects:
    entities  the library-book rows, already filtered to visible libraries by the
              controller
    columns   which of `library`, `book`, `callNumber`, `withinLibraryId` to show

  The original also has `borrower`, `checkedOutOn`, `dueOn` and `checkedInOn` branches,
  inherited from the checkout list it was adapted from (its own `@todo` says so). Only
  the publication show page renders it, and it passes three columns, so those four
  branches are unreachable from anything ported here and are left out. A future port
  that needs them should bring them back rather than pass a column this template drops.

  Two behaviours reproduced rather than tidied:

  1. **The unavailable row is `class="danger"`**, and its call-number cell additionally
     says "(Currently checked out)". Both come from the same `isAvailable` flag, so a
     row can be red *and* say why.
  2. **The heading is always "Physical copy availability"**, and the empty case still
     renders the panel with a sentence inside it. A publication nobody holds shows the
     panel saying so, which is information; hiding it would look like the lookup failed.

  The sortable-table assets are appended here through the layout's blocks rather than by
  `headScript()`/`headLink()`, which is the same pair of files in the same order.
#}
{% set names = {
    'library':         'Library',
    'book':            'Book',
    'callNumber':      'Call number',
    'withinLibraryId': 'Barcode',
} %}
<div class="panel panel-default">

<div class="panel-heading">
    <h3 class="panel-title">{{ translate('Physical copy availability') }}</h3>
</div>

{% if entities is not empty %}
<div id="book-list" class="table-responsive panel-body">
    <table class="table sortable">
        <thead>
        <tr>
            {% for col in columns %}
                <th>{{ translate(names[col]) }}</th>
            {% endfor %}
        </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
        {% for entity in entities %}
        <tr {% if not entity.isAvailable %}class="danger"{% endif %}>
            {% for col in columns %}
{%- if col == 'library' %}
            <td>{{ format_entity('library', entity.library, {'displayEditPencil': false}) }}</td>
{%- elseif col == 'book' %}
            <td>{{ format_entity('book', entity) }}</td>
{%- elseif col == 'callNumber' %}
            <td>{{ entity.callNumber|default('') }}{% if not entity.isAvailable %} {{ translate('(Currently checked out)') }}{% endif %}</td>
{%- elseif col == 'withinLibraryId' %}
            <td>{{ entity.withinLibraryId|default('') }}</td>
{%- endif %}
            {% endfor %}
</tr>{% endfor %}</tbody>
    </table>
</div>
{% else %}
<div class="panel-body">{{ translate('No physical copies available in current library catalogs.') }}</div>
{% endif %}
</div>
